# Architecture

> What "good work" means in this project.

---

## 1. Project overview

{{PROJECT_NAME}} is built with **{{STACK}}**. Describe the product in one
paragraph: what it does, who consumes it, and what is explicitly out of scope.

Design goals:

- **Deterministic** — same input, same output.
- **Observable** — failures are visible and actionable.
- **Small surface** — new modules are added only when this document describes
  their home.
- **Safe** — no secrets in source, no unsafe defaults, no hidden I/O.

---

## 2. Layout

```text
{{LAYOUT_TREE}}
```

Rules:

- One folder per feature/module; kebab-case names.
- Every source file has a documented home; a new folder requires a docs update
  first.
- Tests live next to the code they protect (or in the project's documented
  test tree).
- Generated output never lives in source directories.

---

## 3. Layers

| Layer            | Contents | May import from |
| ---------------- | -------- | --------------- |
| {{LAYERS_TABLE}} |

Dependencies flow top-down. No cycles. I/O belongs at the boundary layer, not
inside pure logic.

---

## 4. State and data

- Server state lives behind the service/client layer.
- Component/UI state is derived from the smallest possible source.
- No global mutable singletons outside the project's dependency-injection
  mechanism.
- Persisted data has an explicit schema and a migration policy.

---

## 5. Quality gates

{{QUALITY_GATES}}

The harness derives a **level** from the task type. Light runs changed
format/lint plus structure/docs; medium adds the affected type check and
targeted specs; full runs every gate above. `docs/harness/verification.md` is
the source of truth for the matrix; `AGENTS.md` has the short version.
